  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Fish Catch Data from the Western Bering Sea and Chukchi Sea Sampled by the R/V TINRO during the Summer and Fall 2003",
  "description": "Salmon and other pelagic nekton were collected in the western Bering Sea and Chukchi Sea by the Russian R/V TINRO from July to October 2003. The Russian trawl vessel R/V TINRO used pelagic rope trawl that was towed with the headrope at the surface (0 m; 1 hr at 3.5-5.0 knots) to sample 172 stations. Salmon catch data includes chum, sockeye, pick, coho, and chinook salmon.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To collect fish as part of the BASIS survey of the Bering Sea.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23569214",
